B.a39=s(["The fibs/PSWs prove there is severe active, ongoing denervation.","The huge MUAPs prove this has been happening essentially forever (the remaining axons have taken over orphaned fibers).","The fasciculations highlight the hallmark irritability of the dying anterior horn cells.","Reduced recruitment occurs because entire motor units are dead."],t.s)
B.KW=new A.ox("case1","Case 1: Motor Neuron Disease","A 55-year-old male presenting with progressive, painless, asymmetric limb weakness and visible twitching in his arms.","Abundant (3+) fibrillations and PSWs in three limbs, extremely large duration and high-amplitude polyphasic MUAPs, profoundly reduced recruitment, and frequent fasciculations.",B.a39)
