B.aFk=new A.ic("Fibrillation Potential","Rain on a tin roof","Biphasic with positive initial deflection. 1-5 ms duration, <300 uV amplitude. Regular firing at 1-10 Hz. Indicates active denervation -- a single muscle fiber spontaneously discharging after losing its nerve supply.",B.fx)
B.aFh=new A.ic("Positive Sharp Wave","Dull thud","Positive initial deflection followed by slow negative phase. 10-30 ms duration, <1 mV amplitude. Regular at 1-20 Hz. Same clinical significance as fibrillations -- active denervation.",B.fx)
B.aFp=new A.ic("Complex Repetitive Discharge","Motor boat","Repeating complex waveform with abrupt onset and cessation. 10-100 Hz, uniform morphology. Spreads by ephaptic transmission between adjacent muscle fibers. Seen in chronic denervation and some myopathies.",B.fx)
B.aFl=new A.ic("Myotonic Discharge","Dive bomber","Waxing and waning amplitude and frequency (20-100 Hz). Due to abnormal muscle membrane ion channel function. Seen in myotonic dystrophy, myotonia congenita, paramyotonia, acid maltase deficiency.",B.aN)
B.aFo=new A.ic("Fasciculation Potential","Corn popping","MUAP-like morphology firing at irregular intervals (<1-2 Hz). Originates from the motor neuron. Pathologic when accompanied by fibrillations/PSWs. Cannot distinguish benign from pathologic on EMG alone.",B.fx)
B.aFr=new A.ic("Normal MUAP","Crisp thud","Triphasic morphology, 5-15 ms duration, 0.1-2 mV amplitude, 2-4 phases. Represents synchronized firing of all muscle fibers in one motor unit. Rise time <500 us indicates electrode is close to the discharging fibers.",B.bz)
B.aFi=new A.ic("Neuropathic MUAP","Thick thud","Long duration (>15 ms), high amplitude (>2 mV), polyphasic (>4 phases). Represents collateral sprouting -- surviving motor neurons adopt orphaned muscle fibers, enlarging the motor unit territory.",B.at)
B.aFm=new A.ic("Myopathic MUAP","Soft crackle","Short duration (<5 ms), low amplitude (<0.5 mV), polyphasic. Motor unit has fewer functioning muscle fibers due to necrosis or splitting. Early recruitment -- more MUAPs needed to generate force.",B.aG)
B.aFn=new A.ic("Endplate Noise (MEPPs)","Sea shell murmur","Irregular, low-amplitude baseline undulation at ~150 Hz. Monophasic negative deflections, 10-50 uV. Normal finding -- indicates needle tip is at the motor endplate zone. This area is painful for the patient.",B.fx)
B.aFj=new A.ic("Endplate Spike","Sputtering fat in frying pan","Biphasic with NEGATIVE initial deflection, 50-100 Hz, irregular. 2-4 ms duration, <1 mV. Provoked by needle irritation at the endplate. The negative initial deflection distinguishes it from fibrillation potentials.",B.fx)
B.aFq=new A.ic("Decremental Response (RNS)","N/A","Progressive drop in CMAP amplitude with slow-rate (2-3 Hz) repetitive stimulation. >10% decrement from 1st to 4th/5th response is abnormal. Classic U-shaped pattern in myasthenia gravis.",B.ak)
B.aFg=new A.ic("Incremental Response (RNS)","N/A",">100% increase in CMAP amplitude after brief exercise or high-rate stimulation. Hallmark of Lambert-Eaton myasthenic syndrome (presynaptic NMJ disorder).",B.ag)
