B.ags=new A.aY("A patient's median motor distal latency is 4.3 ms (upper limit of normal: 4.2 ms) but they have zero hand symptoms. What is the most appropriate interpretation?",B.a3t,2,"Specificity is King. A borderline finding that does not correlate with the patient's symptoms is most likely a normal variant. Labeling a healthy person with CTS based on a 0.1 ms difference could lead to unnecessary surgery.")
B.ZS=s(["Calibrate the machine, test the stimulator, check the filters","Review the MRI, order labs, consult neurology","Take a clinical history, perform a physical exam, formulate a differential diagnosis","Warm the limb, check impedance, set the gain"],t.s)
B.agC=new A.aY("Before turning on the EMG machine, what three steps should the physician always complete?",B.ZS,2,"The Patient Encounter workflow is: (1) Clinical History, (2) Physical Exam, and (3) Differential Diagnosis. The machine comes AFTER you know what questions to ask the nervous system.")
B.a52=s(["The MRI is wrong","The SNAP test was performed incorrectly","The dorsal root ganglion (DRG) is proximal to the lesion, so peripheral sensory axons survive","Sensory nerves are not affected by radiculopathy"],t.s)
B.agJ=new A.aY("A patient has a confirmed C7 radiculopathy on MRI. The median SNAP recorded from the index finger is completely normal. Why?",B.a52,2,"The DRG sits outside the spinal canal. In radiculopathy, the compression is proximal (behind) the DRG. Since the sensory cell body in the DRG is still connected to its peripheral axon, the SNAP remains normal.")
B.a72=s(["The myelin sheath (insulation)","The neuromuscular junction (handshake)","The anterior horn cell (motor neuron cell body)","The muscle fiber itself"],t.s)
B.agq=new A.aY("In Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), which component of the motor unit is primarily affected?",B.a72,2,"ALS is a motor neuron disease -- it destroys the cell body in the anterior horn of the spinal cord. This leads to widespread denervation with fasciculations and fibrillations on EMG with normal sensory studies.")
B.a4N=s(["No recovery is possible","Weeks (remyelination)","6-12 months (axon regrowth)","Years (surgical repair required)"],t.s)
B.agj=new A.aY("A nerve injury causes the myelin to be stripped but the axon remains intact. What is the expected recovery timeline?",B.a4N,1,"Demyelination recovers in weeks because the body can re-wrap myelin relatively quickly. The axon itself is intact, so no regrowth is needed.")
B.a0X=s(["Report the finding as carpal tunnel syndrome","Add a correction factor of 0.2 ms per degree","Warm the hand to at least 32 degrees C and repeat the study","The temperature does not affect distal latency"],t.s)
B.ag1=new A.aY("You record a median motor distal latency of 5.2 ms. The patient's hand skin temperature is 28 degrees C. What should you do?",B.a0X,2,"Cold temperature slows sodium channel kinetics, artificially prolonging latencies. The hand must be warmed to at least 32 degrees C before results can be trusted.")
B.a0U=s(["The nerve is severely damaged","60 Hz electrical interference from building wiring","The stimulator is malfunctioning","The patient is moving too much"],t.s)
B.ah1=new A.aY("You see a thick, rhythmic 'fuzzy' baseline obscuring all your waveforms. What is the most likely cause?",B.a0U,1,"60 Hz interference is the most common artifact in the EMG lab. Fix it by scrubbing the skin to reduce impedance and ensuring good ground electrode contact.")
B.a5r=s(["Nerve conduction shocks will trigger the ICD","The EMG machine will interfere with the pacemaker function","Needle EMG electrical activity near the device may be sensed as a cardiac arrhythmia by the ICD","EMG is absolutely contraindicated in all patients with cardiac devices"],t.s)
B.agg=new A.aY("A patient with an ICD needs an EMG study. What is the primary safety concern?",B.a5r,2,"The primary concern with ICDs is that electrical activity from needle EMG near the generator may be misinterpreted by the device as ventricular fibrillation, potentially triggering an inappropriate shock.")
B.a6z=s(["Ulnar nerve at the elbow","Lower trunk of the brachial plexus","C8 nerve root (radiculopathy)","Guyon's canal at the wrist"],t.s)
B.agS=new A.aY("A patient presents with hand weakness. The ulnar SNAP is absent. Where can the lesion NOT be located?",B.a6z,2,"In radiculopathy, the lesion is proximal to the DRG (preganglionic). The sensory cell bodies remain connected to their peripheral axons, so the SNAP is PRESERVED. An absent SNAP means the lesion is postganglionic.")
B.a44=s(["Carpal tunnel syndrome","ALS (motor neuron disease)","Neuromuscular junction disorder (e.g., myasthenia gravis)","Demyelinating polyneuropathy"],t.s)
