B.Zq=s(["Radial nerve -- posterior forearm","Musculocutaneous nerve -- lateral forearm","Axillary nerve -- regimental badge area","Suprascapular nerve -- posterior shoulder"],t.s)
B.agF=new A.aY("A patient sustains an anterior shoulder dislocation. Which nerve is most at risk, and what is the key sensory area to test?",B.Zq,2,"The axillary nerve (C5-C6, posterior cord) wraps around the surgical neck of the humerus through the quadrilateral space. Anterior shoulder dislocations stretch or compress the nerve. Test sensation over the lateral deltoid ('regimental badge' area).")
B.a6U=s(["Greater sciatic foramen","Piriformis muscle","Popliteal fossa","Fibular head"],t.s)
B.agN=new A.aY("The sciatic nerve bifurcates into its two terminal branches at which anatomical landmark?",B.a6U,2,"The sciatic nerve (L4-S3) typically divides into the tibial nerve and common fibular (peroneal) nerve at or just above the popliteal fossa behind the knee. In approximately 10-15% of individuals, the division occurs higher.")
B.a5X=s(["Sinus tarsi","Tarsal tunnel","Cuboid tunnel","Plantar fascia"],t.s)
B.agy=new A.aY("The tibial nerve passes through which structure at the ankle, analogous to the carpal tunnel at the wrist?",B.a5X,1,"The tarsal tunnel is formed by the flexor retinaculum behind the medial malleolus. The tibial nerve passes through this space. Compression here causes tarsal tunnel syndrome with burning pain and numbness on the plantar surface of the foot.")
B.a_o=s(["It crosses over bone with minimal soft tissue protection","It passes through a tight muscular tunnel","It has poor blood supply at this location","It divides into multiple branches here"],t.s)
B.aga=new A.aY("Why is the common fibular (peroneal) nerve particularly vulnerable to injury at the fibular head?",B.a_o,0,"The common fibular nerve wraps around the fibular neck just beneath the skin with almost no cushioning from muscle or fat. This makes it the most commonly injured nerve in the lower extremity. Compression from leg crossing, casts, or prolonged bed rest can cause foot drop.")
B.a0k=s(["Obturator nerve","Sciatic nerve","Femoral nerve","L3 nerve root"],t.s)
B.ag7=new A.aY("A patient cannot extend the knee and has an absent patellar reflex. Sensation is reduced on the anterior thigh and medial leg. Which nerve is affected?",B.a0k,2,"The femoral nerve (L2-L4) innervates the quadriceps (knee extension), and its terminal sensory branch (saphenous nerve) supplies the medial leg. The patellar reflex is mediated by the femoral nerve (L3-L4). Common causes include retroperitoneal hematoma and post-surgical injury.")
B.ZZ=s(["Greater sciatic foramen","Obturator foramen/canal","Inguinal canal","Femoral triangle"],t.s)
B.ah8=new A.aY("The obturator nerve exits the pelvis through which anatomical structure?",B.ZZ,1,"The obturator nerve (L2-L4) exits through the obturator canal in the pelvis to reach the medial thigh. It innervates the adductor muscles. Obturator neuropathy can occur from pelvic fractures, hip surgery, or obturator hernia.")
B.a6B=s(["Tibial and femoral nerves","Common fibular and tibial nerves","Saphenous and tibial nerves","Superficial and deep fibular nerves"],t.s)
