b9=A.cd(ac7,c1,k0,"INDICATED (To rule out large-fiber involvement)",A.a([A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,g9,h0,f0,f0,h1,f0),A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,h5,h6,f0,f0,h1,f0),A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,l5,l6,f0,f0,q3,f0),A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,m4,m5,f0,f0,m6,f0),A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,m7,m8,f0,f0,m9,f0),A.t(!1,f0,f0,f0,f0,f0,n3,f0,f0,f0,f0,k6)],n),"Pure small fiber neuropathy (SFN) affects the A-delta (thinly myelinated) and C (unmyelinated) fibers responsible for pain and temperature. Because standard NCS/EMG only measures large, myelinated fibers (A-alpha/A-beta), the studies are expected to be **ENTIRELY NORMAL** in pure SFN. Diagnosis is clinical or confirmed by skin biopsy (Intraepidermal Nerve Fiber Density).",c0,"small_fiber",c2,ae8,ae7,!0,b9,A.a(["Small fiber neuropathy (SFN) is a clinical diagnosis characterized by burning pain and loss of pinprick/temperature sensation.","NCS and needle EMG measure ONLY large, myelinated fibers (A-alpha and A-beta).","In pure SFN, the NCS and EMG will be **ENTIRELY NORMAL**.","Associated clinical features include normal strength, normal reflexes, and normal vibration/proprioception (as these are large fiber functions).","Underlying causes include diabetes/pre-diabetes, Sjogren's, HIV, and amyloidosis."],af3),"Burning Feet with Normal Strength")
ae7=A.cc(45,"8-month history of burning pain and numbness in the sole of the foot",d5,"Symptoms worse at night and after prolonged standing (8-12 hour shifts). Some relief with elevation. No back pain. History of ankle sprain 1 year ago.","Ibuprofen","Nurse",i4)
ae8=A.ci("Normal bulk. Mild swelling posterior to medial malleolus.","Tenderness over the tarsal tunnel.","Achilles and Patellar reflexes 2+ and symmetric.","Full ROM at ankle.","Decreased sensation in medial and lateral plantar distributions. Sural distribution (lateral foot) is spared.","Positive Tinel's sign posterior to medial malleolus.","Abductor hallucis 4/5. Other foot muscles 5/5.")
c2=A.a([A.Q(ac9,d9),A.Q(ad0,"S1 radiculopathy would typically cause an absent Achilles reflex and denervation in proximal S1 muscles (Gastrocnemius, Gluteus Maximus); here both are normal."),A.Q(ac8,"Primarily a pain syndrome at the calcaneal insertion; would not cause the significant intrinsic muscle denervation and plantar NCS abnormalities seen here."),A.Q(ac1,"Usually presents with symmetric 'stocking-glove' distribution and abnormal Sural SNAPs; here findings are focal and the Sural is normal."),A.Q(p7,"Sciatic lesions would involve the peroneal division (TA, EHL) and the Sural SNAP; here those are entirely spared.")],ae9)
c0=A.af(["constitutional",n5,"musculoskeletal","Burning pain in the sole of the right foot. No back or hip pain.","neurological","Numbness on the bottom of the foot. Normal strength in the calf and thigh. Normal bowel and bladder function."],af1,af1)
